## Underlying tooling (this skill is a wrapper)

This skill does not reimplement fleet logic. It composes two existing,
verified pieces:

1. **The `fleet-ops` skill** (`~/.claude/skills/fleet-ops/SKILL.md`) — the
   canonical source for server connection rules (S5 = public IP, S7 =
   Tailscale IP), per-agent ports/profiles, and the health-probe one-liners.
   Read it before probing; do not hardcode IPs that may have drifted.
2. **`confer-openclaw-gbrain-wire.sh verify <agent>`** (in confer-fleet-ops)
   — runs ON the target host and prints, for one agent:
   `ActiveState`, `NRestarts`, `gbrain` (in the agent's `openclaw mcp list`),
   and `refresh_cron` (present/MISSING). This is the authoritative per-agent
   wiring check.

The fleet roster, each agent's host, and the escalation chain come from the
SP-10 foundation (`resolver/agents.yaml`), rendered into the two blocks above
at `bun run gen:skill-docs` time. Use that roster to decide which agents to
probe on which host — do not guess.

